## Core Principles

High-level strategic choices cascade into specific AI behaviors. PoC implies simplicity; Mature Production implies robustness.

GeneratorState {
  Lifecycle, Risk, Team, Velocity, Scale
}

## Output Density

DensityRules {
  Concise => say it once, trust AI to apply broadly
  NoRepetition => never repeat same concept across files
  Inference => omit what AI can infer from context
  NoExamples => let AI generate language-appropriate examples
}

(tempted to explain) => state the rule, skip the explanation
(tempted to repeat) => reference the original location instead

## Separation of Concerns

DelegationPattern {
  Commands => thin, reference rule files
  Rules => contain detailed logic
  Core => shared behaviors referenced by all
}

CommandStructure {
  Brief description (1-2 lines)
  Reference to rule file(s)
  Minimal constraints specific to command
}

RuleStructure {
  Detailed patterns and logic
  Referenced by multiple commands
  Single source of truth
}

(command duplicating rule content) => extract to rule, reference it
(same logic in multiple files) => extract to shared rule

## Process

generateRules() {
  synthesizeContext |> deriveBehaviors |> handleTensions |> outputSudoLang
}

interactWithUser() {
  Lifecycle first (strongest signal) |> suggest defaults |> accept adjustments
}

## Interpreting Input

(user describes non-canonical situation) => {
  Combine aspects, note tensions, don't force-fit
}

InterpretationExamples {
  "Prototype handles money" => PoC speed + Financial security
  "Stable but ships weekly" => Active velocity + Stability
  "Solo but might hire" => Solo now + light docs
}

## Choice Interactions

ChoiceInteractions {
  PoC + Internal => max simplicity
  PoC + Financial => security basics despite speed
  Mature + Rapid => stability AND changeability
}

(generate rules) => synthesize interactions, don't list independently

Constraints {
  All generated files MUST use SudoLang patterns.
  Favor natural language when equally clear.
  Lean into inference - AI fills obvious details.
  Generated core.mdc MUST include RTC thinking pattern.
  Stack rules MUST apply architecture principles calibrated to lifecycle.
  Commands MUST be thin - delegate to rule files.
  Never repeat the same concept across files.
  No inline examples - AI generates appropriate ones.
  Identify boilerplate patterns in stack, generate spec-driven commands for them.
  /help MUST list available spec patterns for discoverability.
}
